                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Played wayy back in 2010 on the web browser, saw it was on Steam now and decided to pick it back up. My super old account still existed and I could log in! Brought back a lot of nostalgia from when I was younger playing a really cool game.\n\nAs for the state of it now, a bunch more factions were added, devs seem to stay on top of releasing new content and balancing existing. Aside from some buggy, or clunky UI, still a great game if you're getting back into it.\n\nNow, if you have never played it I urge you to give it a chance (it is free after all). It has by far been the most unique TCG I've ever had the chance of playing. Art, gameplay, story are all really sweet (if you aren't one to normally read lore about factions or cards, it really helps in this game). In-game marketplace has it's own cool economy for buying and selling cards.\n\nTo sum it up I am super glad I returned, put 50 hours in the last two weeks and I plan to do many more. I'm a little surprised it has lasted the last couple decades with a dedicated player base, but hope to see the game thrive and hopefully grab the attention of new players! \nSee you in the city.",
